A GTK3 control panel for the Intel SST audio driver.

The driver exposes twenty-six sysctls: a parametric equaliser, a limiter,
volume ramps, jack detection and live telemetry. They are perfectly usable
from a shell, but tuning an equaliser by typing sysctl names is miserable, and
the peak meters only mean anything if you can watch them move.

Three tabs plot what the settings actually do, updating as the sliders move:
the combined equaliser response, the limiter's input-against-output curve, and
the ramp shape. Inline help explains each setting in a paragraph and links
into the project documentation. A diagnostics tab gathers everything worth
attaching to a bug report into one copyable block.

Reading needs no privilege. Changing a setting does, since the sysctls are
root-writable only; the panel degrades to a live read-only view rather than
demanding to be run as root.

Interface in English, Polish, German, French and Chinese, following the user's
locale.
